-- title:
--   Theta-adaptedness of a framed family is cut out by a finitely generated ideal
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $g, N, n$, a tuple $\delta : \mathrm{Fin}\,g \to \mathbb{N}$ with every $\delta_i$ nonzero, and a bijection $e$ between $\mathrm{Fin}(N+1)$ and $H(\delta) = \prod_i \mathbb{Z}/\delta_i$. Let $S$ be a commutative ring carrying an element $\zeta$ with $\zeta^{N+1} = 1$ such that $1 - \zeta^{j}$ is a unit for all $0 < j < N+1$, and let $X$ be a framed polarised abelian scheme of type $(g, N, n)$ over $S$: a scheme $A$ with a structure morphism $f : A \to \operatorname{Spec} S$, a commutative relative group law $L$, the abelian-scheme property bundle, all fibres of topological Krull dimension $g$, $2g$ marked $n$-torsion sections that form a basis of the $n$-torsion on every geometric fibre, an invertible module `pol` that is a closed immersion by sections with geometric fibre $H^0$ of rank $N+1$, and a `ProjPresentation` of `pol` over $\mathbb{P}^N_S$ whose structure morphism is a closed immersion and whose $N+1$ global sections form a section basis on the whole space. The assertion is that there is a finitely generated ideal $J \subseteq S$ with the following property: for every commutative ring $T$, every ring homomorphism $\varphi : S \to T$ and every framed polarised abelian scheme $Y$ of the same type over $T$ which is a base change of $X$ along $\varphi$ (a morphism $Y.A \to X.A$ making a pullback square over $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi$, compatible with the group laws and the marked sections, with an isomorphism between the pullback of $X$'s polarisation module and $Y$'s, and with $Y.\mathrm{frame}.\mathrm{toProj}$ followed by the base-change map $\mathbb{P}^N_T \to \mathbb{P}^N_S$ equal to that morphism followed by $X.\mathrm{frame}.\mathrm{toProj}$), one has: $Y$ is theta-adapted for $(\delta, e)$ — that is, there is a Schrödinger frame for $Y.f$, $Y.L$, $Y.\mathrm{pol}$ over the identity base, with sections indexed by $H(\delta)$ forming a basis and with theta-point lifts of translations and of additive characters acting by $\sigma_h \mapsto \sigma_{h+h'}$ and $\sigma_h \mapsto \chi(h)\sigma_h$, whose section at $e(i)$ is the pullback of the $i$-th frame section of $Y$ — if and only if the ideal of $T$ generated by $\varphi(J)$ is zero.
--
--   This expresses that, within a framed family of polarised abelian schemes, the locus where the frame is a Schrödinger (theta) frame of multiplicity type $\delta$ is closed and cut out by a finitely generated ideal of the base, compatibly with arbitrary base change. It is the representability input used by [`AlgebraicGeometry.FramedPolarisedAbelianScheme.exists_ideal_fg_isThetaAdapted_iff_eq_bot`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.FramedPolarisedAbelianScheme.exists_ideal_fg_isThetaAdapted_iff_eq_bot).
